WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
A flashy runner is easy to imagine and much harder to keep alive.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:18.000
ALICE begins where style collides with table reality, in that narrow space where a character concept either becomes a professional or folds under the first real job.

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:27.000
The question is never just which build looks coolest.

4
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:36.000
It is which build can carry the weight, absorb the tradeoffs, and still feel like the runner the player wanted to bring into the shadows.

5
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The numbers should tell a story. What became sharper. What became fragile. What was quietly sacrificed to buy the trick.

6
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Gear is not a shopping list. Chrome is not flavor. Magic is not free.

7
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Every choice leaves a shape on the sheet and a consequence in play. ALICE should not sound like a lecture from above.

8
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:12.000
It should feel like a sharp-eyed coach standing beside the player, pointing at the weak seam before the first bad roll tears it open.

9
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:21.000
By the end, the runner still belongs completely to the player.

10
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:30.000
They are simply clearer, stronger, and more ready for the table to test them.
